The potential vulnerability is related to XML External Entity (XXE) injection. This vulnerability arises when an XML parser processes external entities defined within an XML document. If the `xml_data` parameter is not properly configured to disable external entity processing, an attacker could craft malicious XML input containing external entity declarations that reference sensitive local files or external resources. The parser, by default or misconfiguration, might then attempt to fetch and include the content of these external entities in the processing, potentially leading to information disclosure or denial-of-service attacks.

